distributor. Under Rule 6c-11, the fund's shares trade on an exchange, and the creation/redemption mechanism is reserved for APs.\n\n**The usual alternative** is to sell your shares on the exchange through your broker at the prevailing market price. Your buyer is typically another investor or a market maker. Market makers and APs keep the price close to net asset value (NAV) by creating or redeeming creation units when the price drifts too far from NAV. Your sale price may still be slightly above (premium) or below (discount) NAV, especially for thinly traded funds or during volatile markets.","ttft_ms":1811,"type":"result","duration_ms":3334,"uuid":"498a950c-a7de-40e1-9fa6-fc52c34d399f","ttft_stream_ms":413,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":413,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
